  "notes": "Most of the fleet (737-800 and 737 MAX 8) wears this; several specials fly (e.g. 'Impressions of Istanbul', Eintracht Frankfurt, Star Trek, Crystal Palace). Newest Commons photos of a standard aircraft found were 2024; the scheme hasn't changed since. The far (right) side not checked; assumed symmetric. Each aircraft's registration ending is repeated in blue on the fin tip and nose-gear door; not drawn. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on TC-SMA (2024-06-04): the belly's sweeps drawn as curves; 'SunExpress' lowercase 0.65 of its capitals; the engine title runs most of the cowling.",
  "history": "Replaced Skyarium v1's approximation (a few colors from memory) with the current scheme drawn from dated Commons photos. The 2010 scheme replaced SunExpress's earlier yellow-and-blue livery."
